1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,170
Failed call.

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:03,740
Deducted: zero.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:08,830
Agents pay for every call, even the broken ones.

4
00:00:08,830 --> 00:00:12,650
This agent needs one document checked before it files it.

5
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:16,080
It pays only if the check comes back valid.

6
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:23,780
It puts down zero point five testnet NEAR, and sets a limit: no more than zero point two.

7
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:26,450
Whatever happens, it can’t spend past that.

8
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:28,330
First call.

9
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:30,400
The check comes back valid.

10
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:33,440
The buyer checks the receipt.

11
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:35,470
Same fingerprint, real signature.

12
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:39,670
And only then does the contract take zero point one.

13
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:44,580
That’s the whole trick: the buyer checks, then the contract pays.

14
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,270
Now a call fails.

15
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:51,630
The buyer says so, and the money comes back.

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,180
Held, never taken.

17
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,830
Deducted: zero.

18
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,800
The seller’s own error note proves it failed.

19
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,210
No answer in thirty seconds?

20
00:01:03,210 --> 00:01:04,010
Same deal.

21
00:01:04,010 --> 00:01:05,620
The money comes back.

22
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,600
Someone fiddled with the receipt.

23
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:10,370
See that one letter?

24
00:01:10,370 --> 00:01:13,460
The buyer catches it, and pays nothing.

25
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:15,740
Second good check.

26
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:18,240
That’s the limit reached.

27
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,900
Two good checks, zero point two spent.

28
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:23,560
The budget is gone.

29
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:28,960
One more call, and the contract says no before any money moves.

30
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:33,120
Over budget, refused, on the record.

31
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:35,880
Balance untouched.

32
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:39,110
That’s the limit doing its job.

33
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,280
The buyer checks every receipt.

34
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:46,420
The contract only pays on a receipt the buyer has signed.

35
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,030
Replay it yourself.

36
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:52,080
The link’s in the replies.

37
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:54,570
MeteredPay.

38
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:56,510
Failed call?

39
00:01:56,510 --> 00:01:58,450
Deducted: zero.

